  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_016: scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, acc≈0.542), evidence is very sparse. The most impactful architectural uncertainty is whether the simple avgpool aggregation is sufficient or whether a transformer-based aggregation would better capture inter-feature relationships in the multimodal representation. config_048 changes exactly one factor from config_016 (aggregation: avgpool → transformer) while holding all other settings constant (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion, multiprofile, multimodal). This clean single-factor comparison will isolate the effect of aggregation strategy, which is likely a high-leverage design choice. If transformer aggregation improves accuracy, it opens a strong exploitation path for subsequent experiments; if not, it confirms avgpool is adequate and redirects budget toward other factors (RNA encoder, image encoder, fusion). This is the best use of experiment 2 under limited budget because it reduces uncertainty on a high-impact dimension with minimal confounding."
}

